const SITE_DATA_EN={"SNIPPETS":[{"id":"scout","title":"Annotated Scout · Complete Learning Mod","description":"Start with a complete unit that moves, attacks ground targets, switches ammunition, and counts its shots.","category":"单位基础","level":"入门","icon":"tank","tags":["Complete Unit","Chinese Comments","Memory"],"file":"scout.ini","origin":"Original reference example","note":"The complete original file is included. Fields, types, references, and the shared image path were checked statically; the mod has not been run in the game. It depends on SHARED:debug_marker.png in the target Android 1.15 package, so its appearance is a debug marker.","code":"# 原创教学单位，基于指定 Android 1.15 包的解析器静态核对。\n# 注释使用独立行。不要将整份手册当成 INI 导入。\n\n[core]\n# 唯一内部名称；显示名称可以与它不同。\nname: rwDocScout\nclass: CustomUnitMetadata\n# 加强重复键等加载校验。\nstrictLevel: 1\n# 资金价格、生命、质量和碰撞半径。\nprice: 300\nmaxHp: 220\nmass: 2000\nradius: 11\n# 建造基础用时；实际工厂倍率仍会影响用时。\nbuildSpeed: 8s\ntechLevel: 1\n# 沙盒列表入口。\nshowInEditor: true\ndisplayText: 注释侦察车\ndisplayDescription: 对地测试单位\\n按钮切换弹种，开火时记录射击次数\n# 将此单位添加到内置陆军工厂菜单。\nbuiltFrom_1_name: landFactory\nbuiltFrom_1_pos: 90\n# number 是数值类型，boolean 是布尔类型。\ndefineUnitMemory: number shots, boolean powered\n\n[graphics]\n# 该文件已在目标包 assets/units/shared 中确认存在。\nimage: SHARED:debug_marker.png\ntotal_frames: 1\n# 不需要残骸和额外阴影图片。\nimage_wreak: NONE\nimage_shadow: NONE\n\n[attack]\n# 总体攻击能力与三种目标分类。\ncanAttack: true\ncanAttackFlyingUnits: false\ncanAttackLandUnits: true\ncanAttackUnderwaterUnits: false\nmaxAttackRange: 150\n# 时间字段接受 s；这是一次射击间隔。\nshootDelay: 1s\nturretSize: 6\nturretTurnSpeed: 3\n\n[turret_main]\n# 炮塔位置相对单位中心。\nx: 0\ny: 0\n# 引用 [projectile_shell] 时只写后缀 shell。\nprojectile: shell\n# powered 为真时使用另一个已经定义的射弹。\naltProjectile: poweredShell\naltProjectileCondition: memory.powered\n# 每次开火执行隐藏动作；值是动作名，不是 bool。\nonShoot_triggerActions: countShot\n\n[projectile_shell]\n# 普通弹：直接伤害 18。\ndirectDamage: 18\n# life 是时间读取器，1.5s 对应约 90 帧。\nlife: 1.5s\nspeed: 4\ndrawSize: 1\ncolor: #FFE1B0\n\n[projectile_poweredShell]\n# 另一种弹药，用伤害与颜色变化演示模式切换。\ndirectDamage: 30\nlife: 1.5s\nspeed: 4\ndrawSize: 1.3\ncolor: #80D8FF\n\n[movement]\n# 移动类型是枚举，不能写任意中文名称。\nmovementType: LAND\nmoveSpeed: 1\nmoveAccelerationSpeed: 0.06\nmoveDecelerationSpeed: 0.06\nmaxTurnSpeed: 3\nturnAcceleration: 0.3\n\n[hiddenAction_initialize]\n# 出生事件只负责初始化，避免依赖隐式缺省值。\nautoTriggerOnEvent: created\nsetUnitMemory: shots=0, powered=false\n\n[hiddenAction_countShot]\n# 内存写入不支持 +=，使用读取旧值再赋值。\nsetUnitMemory: shots=memory.shots + 1\n\n[action_toggleMode]\n# 动态文本中的 %{...} 在运行时读取内存。\ntext: 切换弹种；已射击 %{memory.shots} 次\ndescription: 切换普通弹与加强弹。此教学模式不收取资源。\nbuildSpeed: 0\n# 反转布尔值；炮塔会读取新状态选择弹种。\nsetUnitMemory: powered=not memory.powered\n","download":"downloads/examples/Annotated_Scout.rwmod"},{"id":"weapons","title":"Standard or Powered Shells: Conditional Ammunition","description":"The turret reads memory.powered to choose between two defined projectiles.","category":"武器系统","level":"进阶","icon":"crosshair","tags":["altProjectile","Conditional Expression"],"file":"conditional-projectile.ini","origin":"Excerpt from Annotated Scout","note":"This fragment comes from the original scout.ini. It needs a complete unit, a declared powered memory variable, and an initialization action. It cannot be imported on its own.","code":"[turret_main]\nx: 0\ny: 0\nprojectile: shell\naltProjectile: poweredShell\naltProjectileCondition: memory.powered\nonShoot_triggerActions: countShot\n\n[projectile_shell]\ndirectDamage: 18\nlife: 1.5s\nspeed: 4\ndrawSize: 1\ncolor: #FFE1B0\n\n[projectile_poweredShell]\ndirectDamage: 30\nlife: 1.5s\nspeed: 4\ndrawSize: 1.3\ncolor: #80D8FF"},{"id":"counter","title":"Count Every Shot","description":"Declare typed memory, initialize it when the unit is created, and call a hidden action whenever the turret fires.","category":"动作逻辑","level":"进阶","icon":"bolt","tags":["setUnitMemory","hiddenAction"],"file":"shot-counter.ini","origin":"Excerpt from Annotated Scout","note":"Merge this code into the matching sections of a complete unit. Do not declare the same variable twice. setUnitMemory does not support +=; read the previous value and assign the result with =.","code":"[core]\ndefineUnitMemory: number shots, boolean powered\n\n[hiddenAction_initialize]\nautoTriggerOnEvent: created\nsetUnitMemory: shots=0, powered=false\n\n[turret_main]\n# 其余炮塔配置仍需保留\nonShoot_triggerActions: countShot\n\n[hiddenAction_countShot]\nsetUnitMemory: shots=memory.shots + 1"},{"id":"toggle","title":"Switch Firing Modes with One Button","description":"Toggle a boolean memory value and display the running shot count on the button.","category":"动作逻辑","level":"进阶","icon":"energy","tags":["action","Dynamic Text"],"file":"toggle-mode.ini","origin":"Excerpt from Annotated Scout","note":"The shots and powered variables must already be declared and initialized. %{...} is for fields that support dynamic text; it is different from the ${...} substitution performed when a unit loads.","code":"[action_toggleMode]\ntext: 切换弹种；已射击 %{memory.shots} 次\ndescription: 切换普通弹与加强弹。此教学模式不收取资源。\nbuildSpeed: 0\nsetUnitMemory: powered=not memory.powered"},{"id":"resource","title":"Resources and Memory: Two Separate Systems","description":"Spend credits to collect a team resource while tracking the number of collections in unit memory.","category":"建筑经济","level":"进阶","icon":"building","tags":["global_resource","price"],"file":"resource_memory_fragment.ini.txt","origin":"Original reference fragment","note":"Merge this original resource and memory fragment into a complete unit. Initialize collected when the unit is created. The spendData action needs an existing energyMax configuration to restore useful energy. The data resource and memory.collected belong to different namespaces.","code":"# 片段：合并到已有完整单位文件，不能作为独立单位导入。\n# 若原文件已有同名节/声明，应合并内容，避免重复键。\n\n[core]\n# 资源与内存是不同系统。声明内存用于记录本单位状态。\ndefineUnitMemory: number collected\n\n[global_resource_data]\n# data 为全队共享资源的内部名。\ndisplayName: 数据\n# HUD 显示适用于此处的全局资源。\ndisplayInHUD: true\n\n[action_collectData]\ntext: 收集数据\n# price 使用静态资源成本语法。\nprice: credits=100\nbuildSpeed: 1s\n# 同样的资源名称在资源表里使用，不能写 memory.data。\naddResources: data=1\n# 内存用 = 写入；计数增加 1。\nsetUnitMemory: collected=memory.collected + 1\n\n[action_spendData]\ntext: 消耗数据\nprice: data=1\nbuildSpeed: 0\naddResources: energy=10\n# 需要接收单位另有 energyMax 等能量配置才有实际恢复意义。\n"},{"id":"map","title":"Spawn Two Reinforcement Tanks After 10 Seconds","description":"Use a TMX unitAdd object to spawn units for team 0 at a chosen location.","category":"地图触发","level":"进阶","icon":"radar","tags":["TMX","unitAdd","XML"],"file":"map_trigger_fragment.xml","origin":"Original reference fragment","note":"This is an object-group fragment, not a complete map. Merge it into an existing triggers group and make sure team 0 exists. The complete TMX still needs terrain, dimensions, and map information.","code":"<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<!-- 这是对象组片段，不是独立地图。合入完整 TMX 时应合并已有 triggers 组。 -->\n<!-- XML object 的 type 决定触发器类型，properties 才是具体参数。 -->\n<objectgroup name=\"triggers\">\n  <!-- 地图开始后 10 秒，在此位置为已存在的队伍 0 生成两辆 tank。 -->\n  <object name=\"doc_spawn\" type=\"unitAdd\" x=\"200\" y=\"200\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\">\n    <properties>\n      <property name=\"team\" value=\"0\"/>\n      <property name=\"delay\" value=\"10s\"/>\n      <property name=\"repeatCount\" value=\"1\"/>\n      <property name=\"spawnUnits\" value=\"tank*2\"/>\n      <property name=\"globalMessage\" value=\"示例增援已经抵达\"/>\n    </properties>\n  </object>\n</objectgroup>\n"},{"id":"inherit","title":"Reuse Turret Settings with Section Templates","description":"Use a template section and @copyFromSection to maintain shared settings in one place.","category":"单位基础","level":"进阶","icon":"layers","tags":["template","Preprocessing"],"file":"section-template.ini","origin":"Excerpt from handbook chapter 5","note":"This learning fragment needs a complete unit and a projectile_shell definition. Section inheritance uses a different syntax from file inheritance through core.copyFrom.","code":"[template_weapon]\ndelay: 1s\n\n[turret_main]\n@copyFromSection: template_weapon\nx: 0\ny: 0\nprojectile: shell"},{"id":"animation","title":"A Gentle Pulsing Idle Animation","description":"Use keyframes to give the unit body a simple back-and-forth scale animation.","category":"图像动画","level":"进阶","icon":"layers","tags":["animation","Keyframes"],"file":"pulse-animation.ini","origin":"Excerpt from handbook chapter 8","note":"Merge this into a complete unit. Body keyframes support scale and frame; legs, turrets, and effects have different keyframe fields.","code":"[animation_pulse]\nonActions: idle\npingPong: true\nbody_0s: {scale:1}\nbody_1s: {scale:1.1}"},{"id":"modinfo","title":"Name the Mod and Set Its Minimum Version","description":"The original learning mod's mod-info.txt belongs in the root of the mod folder.","category":"模组配置","level":"入门","icon":"file","tags":["mod-info","Project Structure"],"file":"mod-info.txt","origin":"Original reference example","note":"The complete original file is included as UTF-8 plain text. It declares the mod itself and must not be merged into a unit's [core] section.","code":"[mod]\n# 游戏 Mod 管理页显示的标题。\ntitle: Annotated Scout / 中文注释示例\n# 普通静态说明文字。\ndescription: 演示单位配置、炮塔、弹种切换与内存计数。已静态核对，尚未实机验证。\n# 使用与本手册一致的最低版本。\nminVersion: 1.15\n"}],"LESSONS":[{"id":"start","number":"01","title":"Import a Complete Learning Mod First","description":"Begin with Annotated Scout and learn its file structure, dependencies, and verification limits.","time":"10 min","level":"入门","source":"Handbook chapter 3; examples/Annotated_Scout/README.txt","sections":[["Which version does this tutorial cover?","This tutorial follows the Rusted Warfare 1.15 handbook for Android. The reference and examples were checked against configuration readers and game assets, but were not run in the game. Test the examples in the game version you use, since behavior can vary between versions and platforms."],["Download and import the mod","Download the “Annotated Scout .rwmod” example from this site. It is the learning mod included in the Rusted Warfare 1.15 reference, not a copy of the game. Import it through the game’s own mod manager, enable it, and reload the units. Storage locations depend on the device and its permissions, so this tutorial does not prescribe a single Android folder path."],["Meet the three files","Extract the .rwmod archive to find mod-info.txt, units/scout.ini, and README.txt. Read the instructions before changing the configuration. The example uses SHARED:debug_marker.png. That image was confirmed in the target package, but it is a debug marker rather than finished tank artwork.","Annotated_Scout/\n├── README.txt\n├── mod-info.txt\n└── units/\n    └── scout.ini"],["How the unit becomes available","The internal name rwDocScout is used by references; displayText gives the unit its visible name, Annotated Scout, written in Chinese in the original example. showInEditor puts it in the sandbox list. builtFrom_1_name: landFactory adds it to the built-in land factory. This compatibility prefix belongs inside core; it is not a separate section.","[core]\nname: rwDocScout\nclass: CustomUnitMetadata\nstrictLevel: 1\nprice: 300\nmaxHp: 220\nmass: 2000\nradius: 11\nbuildSpeed: 8s\nshowInEditor: true\ndisplayText: 注释侦察车\nbuiltFrom_1_name: landFactory\nbuiltFrom_1_pos: 90"],["Check four things in the game","Look for these results: ① Annotated Scout appears in the sandbox under its original Chinese name; ② the land factory can build it for a base price of 300; ③ it moves and attacks ground targets only; ④ the Switch Ammunition button changes the projectile color and damage behavior, and firing increases the shot count. The original button text is also in Chinese."],["Practice: change one value","Change maxHp: 220 to 300, leave the other settings alone, reload, and record what happens. If an error appears, keep the complete message, including the file, section, and key names. Changing graphics, weapons, and memory at the same time makes errors harder to locate."]]},{"id":"syntax","number":"02","title":"Read INI Files and Avoid Time-Unit Traps","description":"Tell static values from runtime expressions, and understand three different timing rules.","time":"12 min","level":"入门","source":"Handbook chapter 4; reference/unit_fields.json","sections":[["The section gives each setting its context","core handles identity and unit stats, graphics handles images, attack handles attack capabilities, and movement handles motion. Sections such as turret_NAME, projectile_NAME, and action_NAME use a suffix to name an instance. NAME, N, and TIME are documentation placeholders; do not copy placeholder braces into a configuration file."],["Put comments on their own lines","Use key: value consistently. Put comments on separate lines beginning with # instead of appending explanations to numeric values. A color such as #FFE1B0 belongs in the value position. strictLevel: 1 helps catch issues such as duplicate keys. When merging code, avoid pasting a whole section twice.","[core]\n# 最大生命值；说明放在单独一行\nmaxHp: 220\n\n[projectile_shell]\ncolor: #FFE1B0"],["Unit time and build rate are different","For unit fields typed as “time (frames or s),” a bare value of 60 is about one second; 1s is also about 60 logic frames. A bare buildSpeed value is a completion fraction per frame instead: 0.01 takes about 100 frames. A value such as 2s is converted into a base build rate. Builder multipliers can still change the actual time.","# 单位配置中的时间\nshootDelay: 1s\nlife: 1.5s\n\n# core 中的建造速率字段，可显式写秒\nbuildSpeed: 8s"],["Map triggers use another timing rule","Bare delay, warmup, and repeatDelay values in map triggers are milliseconds; these properties also accept ms and s. Therefore, map delay: 1000 and a bare time value of 1000 in a unit INI do not mean the same thing. The unit INI time parser in this package does not implement an ms suffix. Ordinary float fields do not automatically accept s either."],["A numeric field does not always accept expressions","A float field does not necessarily accept memory.x. Only fields whose readers support number expressions can use runtime numeric expressions. Check the type, default handling, and notes in the reference before adding one."],["Practice: explain three values","Explain shootDelay: 60, buildSpeed: 0.01, and map delay=1000. They mean approximately 60 logic frames, a base completion fraction of 0.01 per frame, and a map-trigger delay of 1000 milliseconds, respectively. Do not guess the unit from the field name alone."]]},{"id":"weapons","number":"03","title":"From Ground Attacks to Conditional Ammunition","description":"Follow the scout’s turret, its two projectiles, and the memory condition that selects them.","time":"12 min","level":"进阶","source":"The attack, turret, and projectile sections in the original scout.ini","sections":[["Check targeting permissions first","The example sets canAttack to true, permits ground targets, and rejects air and underwater targets. maxAttackRange is 150 and shootDelay is 1s. If the unit will not fire, first check the target category and distance, then inspect the turret."],["Reference the projectile by its suffix","projectile: shell refers to [projectile_shell]. Do not write projectile: projectile_shell. Likewise, onShoot_triggerActions: countShot uses only the hidden action’s suffix.","[turret_main]\nx: 0\ny: 0\nprojectile: shell\naltProjectile: poweredShell\naltProjectileCondition: memory.powered\nonShoot_triggerActions: countShot"],["Define both projectiles","The standard shell has directDamage: 18, while poweredShell has directDamage: 30. Both use life: 1.5s and speed: 4, with different colors. The turret uses the powered shell when powered is true. This condition depends on the memory declaration and initialization in the next lesson, so copying only the turret is not enough."],["Observe a complete attack","Place an enemy ground target and compare the standard and powered shells: their colors, hits, and shot counts. Then place an air target to check that anti-air attacks are disabled. Armor and other target mechanics affect health loss, so a projectile’s directDamage is not necessarily the final damage dealt to every target."],["Practice: trace the dependency chain","Trace “the button changes powered → the turret reads the condition → a projectile is selected → firing calls countShot → shots is updated.” If one step has no effect, check its reference name, value type, and trigger first."]]},{"id":"memory","number":"04","title":"Memory and Buttons: Give a Unit State","description":"Declare, initialize, read, and update memory to build a clear state cycle.","time":"15 min","level":"进阶","source":"Handbook chapters 6 and 7; the action sections in the original scout.ini","sections":[["Declare the right types first","The example declares number shots and boolean powered. number/float and bool/boolean are declaration aliases confirmed by the reference; that does not make int or string[] valid memory declarations. Each value written to memory must match its declared type.","[core]\ndefineUnitMemory: number shots, boolean powered\n\n[hiddenAction_initialize]\nautoTriggerOnEvent: created\nsetUnitMemory: shots=0, powered=false"],["A hidden action needs a way to run","Defining a hiddenAction does not make it run automatically. The created event triggers initialize, and the turret’s onShoot_triggerActions calls countShot. autoTrigger can also use a condition, but an action may keep running while that condition stays true. Use a state check or cooldown when appropriate."],["Do not mix assignment rules","setUnitMemory supports only =, not += or -=. To add one, explicitly read the old value and assign the result. setUnitStats uses a different writer; its supported operators do not apply to unit memory.","[hiddenAction_countShot]\nsetUnitMemory: shots=memory.shots + 1"],["Show state with dynamic text","The button’s %{memory.shots} is evaluated at runtime. Clicking the action toggles powered. Use %{...} only in fields that support dynamic text, and keep it distinct from the ${...} substitution performed when the configuration loads.","[action_toggleMode]\ntext: 切换弹种；已射击 %{memory.shots} 次\ndescription: 切换普通弹与加强弹。此教学模式不收取资源。\nbuildSpeed: 0\nsetUnitMemory: powered=not memory.powered"],["Expressions are still a limited language","You can combine and, or, not, comparisons, and basic arithmetic. = assigns a value; == compares values. This language does not run arbitrary script imports, for/while loops, or Java methods. Check supported functions and parameters in the registration reference."],["Practice: reproduce a visible result","Record the button text when the unit is created. Fire three times, check the counter, switch modes, and keep firing. Note the actual results, game version, and whether the unit was reloaded. If the counter does not increase, check the countShot call and variable names. If the button text is empty, check dynamic text support and the memory types."]]},{"id":"resources","number":"05","title":"Resources, Memory, and Energy Use Different Namespaces","description":"Build a paid collection action using the original resource fragment.","time":"12 min","level":"进阶","source":"Handbook chapter 7; examples/resource_memory_fragment.ini.txt","sections":[["Three kinds of names have different jobs","[global_resource_data] declares the team resource data. memory.collected records state on an individual unit. energy is the unit’s energy resource. These are not the same variable, and memory.data cannot replace a resource cost."],["Merge the declaration and add initialization","Add collected to the existing defineUnitMemory declaration instead of adding a second key with the same name. Add collected=0 to the existing creation-time initialization action. If other actions also use the created event, check whether they write to the same variable.","[core]\ndefineUnitMemory: number shots, boolean powered, number collected\n\n[hiddenAction_initialize]\nautoTriggerOnEvent: created\nsetUnitMemory: shots=0, powered=false, collected=0"],["Pay credits to add a team resource","The original collectData action costs credits=100, adds data=1, and increments collected. price uses static resource-cost syntax; do not insert arbitrary memory expressions into it.","# 片段：合并到已有完整单位文件，不能作为独立单位导入。\n# 若原文件已有同名节/声明，应合并内容，避免重复键。\n\n[core]\n# 资源与内存是不同系统。声明内存用于记录本单位状态。\ndefineUnitMemory: number collected\n\n[global_resource_data]\n# data 为全队共享资源的内部名。\ndisplayName: 数据\n# HUD 显示适用于此处的全局资源。\ndisplayInHUD: true\n\n[action_collectData]\ntext: 收集数据\n# price 使用静态资源成本语法。\nprice: credits=100\nbuildSpeed: 1s\n# 同样的资源名称在资源表里使用，不能写 memory.data。\naddResources: data=1\n# 内存用 = 写入；计数增加 1。\nsetUnitMemory: collected=memory.collected + 1\n\n[action_spendData]\ntext: 消耗数据\nprice: data=1\nbuildSpeed: 0\naddResources: energy=10\n# 需要接收单位另有 energyMax 等能量配置才有实际恢复意义。\n"],["Why spending data may not restore useful energy","spendData costs data=1 and adds energy=10, but the unit also needs energy settings such as energyMax for that increase to have a useful effect. The original fragment states this dependency; it is not a finished unit that can be imported on its own."],["Practice: compare team state and unit state","Create two units of the same type and use one to collect resources. Observe the team’s data total and that unit’s collected value separately. Then try the actions without enough credits or data and check the buttons and payment behavior."]]},{"id":"templates","number":"06","title":"Connect Inheritance, Preprocessing, and Animation","description":"Separate reuse at load time from state at runtime to keep templates understandable.","time":"12 min","level":"进阶","source":"Handbook chapters 5 and 8; reference/dynamic_key_patterns.json","sections":[["Separate file inheritance from section inheritance","copyFrom in [core] reads other configuration files; @copyFromSection reuses another section. Relative paths, ROOT:, and CORE: use different roots. Circular inheritance or excessive inheritance depth will fail. Changes to a shared template affect every definition that references it.","[template_weapon]\ndelay: 1s\n\n[turret_main]\n@copyFromSection: template_weapon\nx: 0\ny: 0\nprojectile: shell"],["Static substitution happens when the unit loads","@global and @define declare static values, and ${...} substitutes them at load time. The maxHp value below is calculated from a static math expression; it does not change with the unit’s runtime state.","[core]\n@global baseHp: 200\nmaxHp: ${baseHp * 2}"],["Keep the two interpolation forms separate","${...} and the %{...} used in dynamic action text are not interchangeable. The reference notes limits on chained static substitutions. Although tan appears in the internal evaluator, that alone does not establish that ${tan(...)} works directly."],["Match keyframe fields to their targets","body_TIME supports scale and frame. Legs and arms can use coordinates, height, and alpha; turret keyframes can use coordinates. Do not mix fields between target types. Mixing keyframe animation with start/end frame-range animation may also be rejected.","[animation_pulse]\nonActions: idle\npingPong: true\nbody_0s: {scale:1}\nbody_1s: {scale:1.1}"],["Practice: begin with a small shared setting","In a complete unit, first use template_weapon to share one turret’s delay, then add a body-scale animation. Load after each change and record which object changes and which action triggers it. Remember that a template fragment is not a standalone unit."]]},{"id":"maps","number":"07","title":"TMX Triggers: Add Reinforcements to a Map","description":"Read object types and properties, then connect the ten-second reinforcement fragment.","time":"15 min","level":"进阶","source":"Handbook chapter 9; examples/map_trigger_fragment.xml","sections":[["Maps use XML, not unit INI","A complete map needs dimensions, terrain, tilesets, and map information. The target package requires orthogonal maps. Its layer-data reader supports base64 with gzip, zlib, or no compression. This does not establish support for every other Tiled format."],["type and properties have separate roles","A normal trigger’s object type selects the trigger, such as unitAdd. Settings including team, delay, and spawnUnits go inside properties. Merge this fragment into an existing triggers object group instead of pasting INI sections into the map.","<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<!-- 这是对象组片段，不是独立地图。合入完整 TMX 时应合并已有 triggers 组。 -->\n<!-- XML object 的 type 决定触发器类型，properties 才是具体参数。 -->\n<objectgroup name=\"triggers\">\n  <!-- 地图开始后 10 秒，在此位置为已存在的队伍 0 生成两辆 tank。 -->\n  <object name=\"doc_spawn\" type=\"unitAdd\" x=\"200\" y=\"200\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\">\n    <properties>\n      <property name=\"team\" value=\"0\"/>\n      <property name=\"delay\" value=\"10s\"/>\n      <property name=\"repeatCount\" value=\"1\"/>\n      <property name=\"spawnUnits\" value=\"tank*2\"/>\n      <property name=\"globalMessage\" value=\"示例增援已经抵达\"/>\n    </properties>\n  </object>\n</objectgroup>\n"],["Understand what the original fragment should do","About ten seconds after the map starts, the fragment should spawn tank*2 at the object position x=200, y=200 for an existing team 0. globalMessage provides a visible message. repeatCount=1 schedules a single occurrence. Check the result inside the complete map."],["Do not mix the two spawn-list formats","spawnUnits uses a list such as tank*2. A survivalWaves list uses “quantity unitType” instead. Wave times after + are integer seconds or minutes:seconds, which is different from the millisecond rule for ordinary map-trigger values.","# 生存波次示意，不是 spawnUnits 值\n+10 第一波 - 3 tank\n+0:30 第二波 [lockSpawn] - 5 tank, 2 hoverTank\n!unlockSpawn"],["Practice: test the trigger inside a complete map","Back up a valid map, merge the fragment, and confirm that the team and unit names exist. Check the message, spawn position, and number of spawns. If the XML parses but nothing happens, also inspect trigger connections and the map mode. Passing an XML check does not prove that a game event ran."]]},{"id":"debug","number":"08","title":"From Static Checks to Reproducible Mod Sharing","description":"Understand evidence grades and prepare a clear, honest handoff for a mod.","time":"10 min","level":"入门","source":"Handbook chapters 1 and 17; reference/verification_report.json","sections":[["What do the evidence grades mean?","A: the target package contains an asset example and a corresponding reader was found. B: a parser or registration exists, but the assets may not use it. C: an original example combines documented interfaces and has passed static checks. None of these grades means the code was run on a device. The original Annotated Scout example is grade C."],["What was actually checked in the reference?","The checks covered archive integrity, descriptions and sources for 984 fields, cross-checks against DEX strings, unit and map asset coverage categories, example fields and static references, XML fragment parsing, and the input ZIP’s CRC and fingerprint. runtime_tested is false in verification_report.json."],["Fix the earliest error first","Check in this order: required files and images → exact section and key names → value types and time units → duplicate keys and inheritance → references to turrets, projectiles, actions, memory, and resources. A string being accepted by a parser does not prove that a matching execution path exists."],["Record three kinds of verification separately","Static checks confirm that files can be read and that fields and references are consistent. Runtime verification means reloading and observing behavior on a stated game version and device. Multiplayer and performance checks additionally examine synchronization and load. Record these separately. This site does not label reference examples as tested in the game."],["State dependencies and permissions when sharing","Include the target version, purpose, file structure, integration points, asset dependencies, author, license, verification scope, and reproduction steps. The site’s “Share Code” tool saves local drafts and exports share cards; it does not claim to submit or publish them automatically. Files can be sent to the site maintainer for inclusion."],["Practice: write a reproducible test record","For example: Android 1.15; import Annotated_Scout.rwmod; create rwDocScout in the sandbox; fire at a ground target three times; expect shots=3; record the actual result and any complete error message. Only after running that test should the result be described as tested in that environment."]]}],"summary":{"field_count":984,"logic_registration_groups":121,"logic_names_with_aliases":143,"mutable_stats":19,"map_properties":88,"mini_language_argument_counts":{"spawnUnits":23,"spawnProjectiles":15,"price":9,"imageStack":2,"animationKeyframe":8},"asset_field_categories":{"direct_field":497,"asset_metadata_not_consumed_by_android_mod_reader":2,"legacy_canBuild_prefix":28,"inactive_comment_section":50,"legacy_action_prefix":11,"legacy_builtFrom_prefix":6,"legacy_graphics_animation_prefix":16,"animation_keyframe":63,"template_requires_destination_context":8},"runtime_tested":false,"manual_chars":269874,"manual_bytes":409897,"hardcoded_unit_types":52,"loaded_builtin_sounds":29,"builtin_effect_strips":20},"sourceDate":"2026-10-17","integratedDate":"2026-10-19"};
